WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.662
On this slide, we are focusing on variables can be reassigned.

00:00:03.662 --> 00:00:08.182
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:14.267
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:17.937
A variable is a meaningful name connected to a value.

00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:21.867
Clear names help the code communicate what the data represents,

00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:25.212
and later calculations can reuse the stored value.

00:00:25.212 --> 00:00:28.392
Connect the concept to a small analytics task.

00:00:28.392 --> 00:00:33.467
Imagine the value came from a sales file, survey, or operational system.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:38.482
Ask whether Python is interpreting it correctly and whether another person could understand the calculation

00:00:38.482 --> 00:00:40.899
from the names and output.
